<title>FRANCE: Rhone-Poulenc Q1 net income up 6.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc Q1 net income up 6.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>(All figures in millions of francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net per share (francs)		    2.05     vs	 1.97</p>
<p>    Net income				     674     vs	  633</p>
<p>    Operating income			   2,001     vs	1,819</p>
<p>    Financial charges			    525     vs	  683</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			     1,526     vs	1,537</p>
<p>    Sales					 21,599     vs     21,129</p>
<p>NOTE - Chairman Jean-Rene Fourtou said in a statement the company maintained its aim of a 20 percent rise in 1997 earnings per share, before exceptionals.  </p>
<p>But he said the objective would be harder to achieve because of the product recall at its Centeon joint venture with Hoechst.</p>
<p>    Profit from subsidiaries		    12     vs	  326</p>
<p>    Taxes					    471     vs	  473</p>
<p>Breakdown of operating income</p>
<p>     - pharmaceuticals			   885     vs	  592</p>
<p>     - animal health			     873     vs	  820</p>
<p>     - chemicals				   328     vs	  377</p>
<p>     - fibres and polymers			94     vs	   75</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc said it would publish its second quarter results on July 25 and its third quarter results on October 30.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
